.TH LOFI 1 "@DATE@" "lofi @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lofi \- Discord bot that plays lofi in a voice channel, with a web dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lofi
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-\-demo\fR]
[\fB\-\-dashboard\-token\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-dashboard\fR]
[\fB\-\-dashboard\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR]
[\fB\-\-dashboard\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-sync\-commands\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-logfile\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lofi
joins a voice channel in a Discord server and plays lofi continuously. It also
serves a token\-authenticated web dashboard on \fB127.0.0.1:8790\fR for
transport control, per\-server settings, stations and history.
.PP
Audio can come from YouTube broadcasts, SomaFM radio streams, your own
\fBmusic/\fR directory, or
.B Studio Lofi
beats rendered locally. The last two work with no network connection.
.PP
The bot token is read from the \fBLOFI_TOKEN\fR environment variable or from
\fIconfig.json\fR in the data directory. It is never bundled in the package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Diagnose the install and exit: reports whether \fBffmpeg\fR and
\fBlibopus\fR are found, where the data directory resolves to, and whether a
token is configured. Does not connect to Discord.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Serve the dashboard with three simulated servers. No token and no Discord
connection required.
.TP
.B \-\-dashboard\-token
Print the dashboard login key and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dashboard
Run the bot without serving the web dashboard.
.TP
.B \-\-dashboard\-host \fIHOST\fR
Bind the dashboard to \fIHOST\fR instead of the configured value.
.TP
.B \-\-dashboard\-port \fIPORT\fR
Bind the dashboard to \fIPORT\fR instead of the configured value.
.TP
.B \-\-sync\-commands
Publish the slash command tree to Discord and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level \fILEVEL\fR
Logging verbosity: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR.
.TP
.B \-\-logfile \fIPATH\fR
Write logs to \fIPATH\fR instead of the data directory.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOFI_TOKEN
The Discord bot token. Required unless it is set in \fIconfig.json\fR.
.TP
.B LOFI_HOME
Data directory for \fIconfig.json\fR, \fIlofi.db\fR and the audio cache.
Defaults to the platform state directory. Set this when running as a service.
.TP
.B LOFI_DASHBOARD_TOKEN
Overrides the dashboard key so it never touches disk.
.TP
.B LOFI_OPUS
Explicit path to the libopus shared library, if auto\-detection fails.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/lofi
The single\-file binary.
.TP
.I /etc/lofi/lofi.env
Environment file for the systemd unit, created from the packaged example
(mode 0600). Holds \fBLOFI_TOKEN\fR.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/lofi.service
systemd unit, installed disabled.
.TP
.I /var/lib/lofi
Default \fBLOFI_HOME\fR when running under systemd.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check the machine before the first run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ lofi \-\-check
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run the bot with the token in the environment:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ LOFI_TOKEN=... lofi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run it as a service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sudo systemctl enable \-\-now lofi
$ journalctl \-u lofi \-f
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
